## Purpose

Ensure Python code is self-explanatory, consistent, and AI-friendly by maintaining clear docstrings, module headers, and helpful inline anchors.

## Documentation Guidelines
	•	Module headers: At the top of every module, add a short """...""" block describing its purpose, role in the system, and core dependencies.
	•	Functions: Every function should have a docstring unless its name is already fully self-explanatory.
	•	Docstring style: Use this structure:
```
"""Short summary.

Args:
    <param>: description
Returns:
    description
"""
```

## Definition of Done
	•	All modules and functions are documented.
	•	AI anchors exist where dependencies or non-obvious logic need highlighting.
